ILLUSTRATIVE ONLY — NOT AN ASSERTION FIXTURE. See contract.md §8.
This grid shows the INTENDED render of contract §3b's fixture: a CJK tab
followed by an ASCII control tab, 80x6. It is deliberately NOT diffed as a
golden grid, because a `.screen` diff cannot see #554's defect at all — the
broken and fixed renders stringify identically through `TuiDriver::screen()`
and differ only in cell striding (contract §2). Every load-bearing assertion
for #554 goes through `find_bounds`, never `screen_contains` or a grid diff.
Intended widths, once #554 is fixed:
  " 1: 日本語.rs "  -> 14 columns   (日本語 = 3 glyphs x 2 columns)
  "日本語.rs"       ->  9 columns   (find_bounds width, contract §3c)
  " 2: main.rs "   -> 12 columns
  "main.rs"        ->  7 columns   (find_bounds width, contract §3d)
